@{c}ZNC Compiler - v0.5
@{c}A Native 'C-Like' Compiler

@{h2}Requirements
znc  - 0.5       zopt - 0.3        asm  - 0.8c       zed  - 0.6a

ZNC is a language and compiler for the ZX Spectrum Next. The language is closely
modeled after the C programming language, but does deviate in some cases where
it either made the language easier to parse or in other cases where the author
(taylorza) preferred an alternate syntax.

The compiler is a non-optimizing single pass compiler, while the generated code
is not the fastest nor the smallest it should out-perform non-compiled
languages.

